{"rank": 8, "word": "ser", "display": "to be", "pos": "verb", "difficulty": "A1", "tags": ["hardcoded", "irregular", "curated"], "notes": "Fundamental copular verb 'to be' (permanent/essential qualities). Used for identity, origin, material, time, passive voice. Contrasts with estar (temporary states/location). Highly irregular: soy, eres, es, somos, sois, son.", "glosses": ["be", "is", "am", "are", "was", "were"], "examples": [{"es": "Ella es profesora de matemáticas.", "en": "She is a maths teacher."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": "ser", "reflexive": null, "gender": null, "plural": null, "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/seɾ/", "syllables": ["ser"], "irregular": true, "conjugation_class": "irregular-ser", "overrides": {"present": ["soy", "eres", "es", "somos", "sois", "son"], "preterite": ["fui", "fuiste", "fue", "fuimos", "fuisteis", "fueron"], "imperfect": ["era", "eras", "era", "éramos", "erais", "eran"], "future": ["seré", "serás", "será", "seremos", "seréis", "serán"], "conditional": ["sería", "serías", "sería", "seríamos", "seríais", "serían"], "subjunctive": ["sea", "seas", "sea", "seamos", "seáis", "sean"], "imperative": ["sean"], "gerund": "siendo", "past_participle": "sido"}}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A1", "rank": 50, "corpus_frequency": 819688}, "domains": ["essential"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "hardcoded", "needs_review": false}
