{"rank": 121, "word": "tal", "display": "such", "pos": "adjective", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Adjective/adverb 'such/so'. Tal vez = perhaps. Con tal de que + subj = as long as. Un tal = a certain (person). Tal cual = exactly as is.", "glosses": ["such", "so"], "examples": [{"es": "No esperaba tal respuesta.", "en": "I didn't expect such an answer."}, {"es": "¿Cómo estás? — Tal cual.", "en": "How are you? — So-so."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": null, "plural": null, "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/tal/", "syllables": ["tal"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 328, "corpus_frequency": 317926}, "domains": ["general"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 122, "word": "fuera", "display": "outside", "pos": "adverb", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["hardcoded", "function_word", "curated"], "notes": "Adverb 'outside/out'. Estar fuera = to be out/abroad. Fuera de = outside of/beyond. ¡Fuera! = Get out! Also imperfect subjunctive of ser/ir: si fuera.", "glosses": ["outside"], "examples": [{"es": "Los niños juegan fuera de la casa.", "en": "The children are playing outside the house."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": null, "plural": null, "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/ˈfwe.ɾa/", "syllables": ["fue", "ra"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 95, "corpus_frequency": 311571}, "domains": ["essential"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "hardcoded", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 123, "word": "después", "display": "after", "pos": "adverb", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["hardcoded", "function_word", "curated"], "notes": "Adverb 'after/later/afterwards'. Después de + inf = after doing. Después de todo = after all. Poco después = shortly after. Contrasts with antes.", "glosses": ["after", "later"], "examples": [{"es": "Te llamo después del trabajo.", "en": "I'll call you after work."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": null, "plural": null, "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/desˈpwes/", "syllables": ["des", "pués"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 96, "corpus_frequency": 311500}, "domains": ["essential"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "hardcoded", "needs_review": false}
