{"rank": 125, "word": "dinero", "display": "money", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Masculine noun 'money'. Ganar/ahorrar dinero = to earn/save money. Sin dinero = without money/broke. Dinero en efectivo = cash. El dinero no lo es todo.", "glosses": ["money"], "examples": [{"es": "No tengo suficiente dinero para pagar el alquiler.", "en": "I don't have enough money to pay the rent."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": "masculine", "plural": "dineros", "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/diˈne.ɾo/", "syllables": ["di", "ne", "ro"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 98, "corpus_frequency": 300518}, "domains": ["general"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 126, "word": "mundo", "display": "world", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Masculine noun 'world'. Todo el mundo = everyone. El mundo entero = the whole world. De todo el mundo = from all over the world. Dar la vuelta al mundo = to travel around the world.", "glosses": ["world"], "examples": [{"es": "Ha viajado por todo el mundo.", "en": "He has travelled all over the world."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": "masculine", "plural": "mundos", "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/ˈmun.do/", "syllables": ["mun", "do"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 99, "corpus_frequency": 298208}, "domains": ["general"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 127, "word": "claro", "display": "clear", "pos": "adjective", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Adjective 'clear/light-colored'. Adverb/interjection 'of course/obviously'. ¡Claro que sí! = Of course! Está claro = it's clear. Claro que no = of course not.", "glosses": ["clear", "of course"], "examples": [{"es": "El mensaje es muy claro.", "en": "The message is very clear."}, {"es": "Claro que sí, con mucho gusto.", "en": "Of course, with pleasure."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": null, "plural": null, "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/ˈkla.ɾo/", "syllables": ["cla", "ro"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 100, "corpus_frequency": 296584}, "domains": ["general"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 128, "word": "momento", "display": "moment", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Masculine noun 'moment'. En este momento = right now/at this moment. Por el momento = for the time being. De momento = for now. En un momento = in a moment.", "glosses": ["moment"], "examples": [{"es": "Espera un momento, enseguida estoy contigo.", "en": "Wait a moment, I'll be right with you."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": "masculine", "plural": "momentos", "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/moˈmen.to/", "syllables": ["mo", "men", "to"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 101, "corpus_frequency": 294559}, "domains": ["general"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 129, "word": "les", "display": "them", "pos": "pronoun", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["hardcoded", "function_word", "curated"], "notes": "Third-person plural indirect object pronoun 'to them/to you (pl formal)'. Les doy = I give them/you. Often combined with se before lo/la: se lo doy. Leísmo (Spain): les for direct object.", "glosses": ["them"], "examples": [{"es": "Les dije la verdad a todos.", "en": "I told everyone the truth."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": null, "plural": null, "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/les/", "syllables": ["les"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 102, "corpus_frequency": 294439}, "domains": ["essential"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "hardcoded", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 130, "word": "estado", "display": "state", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Masculine noun 'state/condition'. Estado civil = marital status. Estado de ánimo = mood. Los Estados Unidos. Also past participle of estar: he estado.", "glosses": ["state", "condition"], "examples": [{"es": "El estado de salud del paciente es estable.", "en": "The patient's health condition is stable."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": "masculine", "plural": "estados", "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/esˈta.do/", "syllables": ["es", "ta", "do"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 329, "corpus_frequency": 292015}, "domains": ["general"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 131, "word": "mañana", "display": "tomorrow", "pos": "adverb", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["hardcoded", "function_word", "curated"], "notes": "Feminine noun 'morning'. Adverb 'tomorrow'. Por la mañana = in the morning. Buenos días/buenas mañanas. Mañana mismo = tomorrow itself. Pasado mañana = the day after tomorrow.", "glosses": ["tomorrow", "morning"], "examples": [{"es": "Mañana por la mañana tengo una entrevista.", "en": "Tomorrow morning I have an interview."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": null, "plural": null, "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/maˈɲa.na/", "syllables": ["ma", "ña", "na"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 104, "corpus_frequency": 283391}, "domains": ["essential", "time"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "hardcoded", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 132, "word": "madre", "display": "mother", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Feminine noun 'mother'. ¡Madre mía! = My goodness! De puta madre (vulgar) = awesome. La madre patria = the motherland. Madre de familia = housewife/mother.", "glosses": ["mother", "mom"], "examples": [{"es": "Su madre la llamó tres veces esta mañana.", "en": "Her mother called her three times this morning."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": "feminine", "plural": "madres", "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/ˈma.ðɾe/", "syllables": ["ma", "dre"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 105, "corpus_frequency": 281646}, "domains": ["general"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
