{"rank": 134, "word": "lugar", "display": "place", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Masculine noun 'place/location'. En lugar de = instead of. Tener lugar = to take place. Dar lugar a = to give rise to. En primer lugar = firstly/in the first place.", "glosses": ["place"], "examples": [{"es": "Este es el lugar perfecto para una foto.", "en": "This is the perfect place for a photo."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": "masculine", "plural": "lugares", "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/luˈɣaɾ/", "syllables": ["lu", "gar"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 106, "corpus_frequency": 280315}, "domains": ["general"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 135, "word": "donde", "display": "where", "pos": "conjunction", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["hardcoded", "function_word", "curated"], "notes": "Relative adverb 'where' (no accent in relative clauses). La ciudad donde nací. En donde = in/at which. Adonde = (to) where. ¿Dónde? = where? (with accent, question).", "glosses": ["where"], "examples": [{"es": "Ese es el restaurante donde nos conocimos.", "en": "That's the restaurant where we met."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": null, "plural": null, "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/ˈdon.de/", "syllables": ["don", "de"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 107, "corpus_frequency": 277524}, "domains": ["essential"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "hardcoded", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 136, "word": "seguro", "display": "sure", "pos": "adjective", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Adjective 'safe/sure/certain'. Noun: el seguro = insurance/safety catch. Por supuesto/seguro = of course. Estar seguro de = to be sure about. Seguro de vida = life insurance.", "glosses": ["sure", "safe"], "examples": [{"es": "Este lugar es completamente seguro.", "en": "This place is completely safe."}, {"es": "Estoy seguro de que vendrá.", "en": "I am sure he will come."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": null, "plural": null, "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/seˈɣu.ɾo/", "syllables": ["se", "gu", "ro"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 108, "corpus_frequency": 277231}, "domains": ["general"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 137, "word": "espera", "display": "wait", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Noun 'wait'. Noun from esperar. Sala de espera = waiting room. En espera de = awaiting/pending. Sin espera = without waiting. Also 3rd sg present: él espera.", "glosses": ["wait", "waiting"], "examples": [{"es": "La espera en el aeropuerto fue muy larga.", "en": "The wait at the airport was very long."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": "feminine", "plural": "esperas", "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/esˈpe.ɾa/", "syllables": ["es", "pe", "ra"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 330, "corpus_frequency": 270741}, "domains": ["general"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 138, "word": "nuevo", "display": "new", "pos": "adjective", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Adjective 'new'. De nuevo = again. Año nuevo = new year. Como nuevo = as good as new. ¿Qué hay de nuevo? = What's new? Nuevo/a precedes noun for 'another': nuevo intento.", "glosses": ["new"], "examples": [{"es": "Tengo un trabajo nuevo.", "en": "I have a new job."}, {"es": "Estrenamos el nuevo coche ayer.", "en": "We broke in the new car yesterday."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": null, "plural": null, "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/ˈnwe.βo/", "syllables": ["nue", "vo"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 109, "corpus_frequency": 269895}, "domains": ["general"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 139, "word": "hijo", "display": "son", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Masculine noun 'son'. Pl: hijos = sons/children. ¡Hijo mío! = My son/dear boy! Hijo único = only child. Hijo de puta (vulgar). Hijastro = stepson.", "glosses": ["son"], "examples": [{"es": "Tiene dos hijos, uno de cinco y otro de ocho años.", "en": "She has two children, one aged five and one aged eight."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": "masculine", "plural": "hijos", "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/ˈi.xo/", "syllables": ["hi", "jo"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 111, "corpus_frequency": 267856}, "domains": ["general"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 140, "word": "allí", "display": "there", "pos": "adverb", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["hardcoded", "function_word", "curated"], "notes": "Adverb 'there (further away)'. Por allí = over there/that way. De allí = from there. Contrasts with aquí (here) and ahí (there, near listener).", "glosses": ["there"], "examples": [{"es": "El banco está allí, al fondo de la calle.", "en": "The bank is there, at the end of the street."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "reflexive": null, "gender": null, "plural": null, "register": "neutral", "ipa": "/aˈʎi/", "syllables": ["a", "llí"], "conjugations": null, "irregular": false}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"band": "A2", "rank": 112, "corpus_frequency": 267215}, "domains": ["essential"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "hardcoded", "needs_review": false}
