{"rank": 1218, "word": "valor", "display": "value / courage", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "B1", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Two main meanings: (1) value/worth — el valor del euro; (2) courage/bravery — tener valor. Valores morales = moral values. Sin valor = worthless / cowardly.", "glosses": ["value", "worth", "courage", "bravery", "price"], "examples": [{"es": "Tuvo mucho valor para decir la verdad.", "en": "He showed great courage in telling the truth."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "gender": "m", "plural": "valores", "conjugations": null, "irregular": false, "register": "neutral", "reflexive": null, "ipa": "", "syllables": []}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": ["valiente", "precio", "valentía"], "synonyms": ["valentía", "coraje"], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"corpus_frequency": 27034, "band": "B1"}, "domains": ["finance", "emotion", "ethics"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
