{"rank": 1228, "word": "defensa", "display": "defence / defence", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "B1", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "En defensa propia = in self-defence. Ministerio de Defensa = Ministry of Defence. In sport: el defensa = defender. La defensa de una tesis = thesis defence.", "glosses": ["defence", "defense", "defender", "protection"], "examples": [{"es": "El abogado preparó la defensa de su cliente.", "en": "The lawyer prepared his client's defence."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "gender": "f", "plural": "defensas", "conjugations": null, "irregular": false, "register": "neutral", "reflexive": null, "ipa": "", "syllables": []}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": ["defender", "protección", "ataque"], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": ["ataque"]}, "frequency": {"corpus_frequency": 24602, "band": "B1"}, "domains": ["legal", "military", "sport"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 1229, "word": "inglés", "display": "English", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "A1", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Hablar inglés = to speak English. El inglés = the English language, or an Englishman. Clase de inglés = English class. Also adjective: una palabra inglesa = an English word.", "glosses": ["English", "English language", "Englishman"], "examples": [{"es": "Habla inglés con mucho acento.", "en": "He speaks English with a strong accent."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "gender": "m", "plural": "ingleses", "conjugations": null, "irregular": false, "register": "neutral", "reflexive": null, "ipa": "", "syllables": []}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": ["español", "francés", "idioma", "lengua"], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"corpus_frequency": 24267, "band": "A1"}, "domains": ["language", "everyday"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 1230, "word": "estudio", "display": "study / studio", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "A2", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Horas de estudio = study hours. Estudio de grabación = recording studio. Apartamento estudio = studio flat. Estudios (plural) = studies/education. Verb: estudiar.", "glosses": ["study", "studio", "survey", "flat", "education"], "examples": [{"es": "Necesita más horas de estudio para aprobar.", "en": "She needs more hours of study to pass."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "gender": "m", "plural": "estudios", "conjugations": null, "irregular": false, "register": "neutral", "reflexive": null, "ipa": "", "syllables": []}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": ["estudiar", "aprendizaje", "educación"], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"corpus_frequency": 24243, "band": "A2"}, "domains": ["education", "everyday", "music"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 1231, "word": "propósito", "display": "purpose / intention", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "B1", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "A propósito = on purpose (intentionally) OR by the way (changing topic). Con el propósito de = with the aim of. Sin propósito = aimlessly. Propósito de año nuevo = New Year's resolution.", "glosses": ["purpose", "intention", "aim", "by the way", "on purpose"], "examples": [{"es": "Lo hizo a propósito para molestarme.", "en": "He did it on purpose to annoy me."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "gender": "m", "plural": "propósitos", "conjugations": null, "irregular": false, "register": "neutral", "reflexive": null, "ipa": "", "syllables": []}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": ["objetivo", "meta", "intención"], "synonyms": ["intención", "fin"], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"corpus_frequency": 24020, "band": "B1"}, "domains": ["everyday", "ethics"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 1232, "word": "metro", "display": "metre / subway", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "A1", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Two main meanings: (1) unit of length — un metro de tela = a metre of fabric; (2) underground railway — coger el metro = to take the subway/tube. Metro cuadrado = square metre.", "glosses": ["metre", "meter", "subway", "underground", "tube"], "examples": [{"es": "Cogemos el metro para ir al centro.", "en": "We take the subway to get to the centre."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "gender": "m", "plural": "metros", "conjugations": null, "irregular": false, "register": "neutral", "reflexive": null, "ipa": "", "syllables": []}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": ["kilómetro", "centímetro", "tren", "autobús"], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"corpus_frequency": 23962, "band": "A1"}, "domains": ["transport", "measurement", "everyday"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
