{"rank": 1237, "word": "contrario", "display": "contrary / opposite", "pos": "adjective", "difficulty": "B1", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Al contrario = on the contrary. Todo lo contrario = quite the opposite. De lo contrario = otherwise. En sentido contrario = in the opposite direction. Also noun: el contrario = the opponent.", "glosses": ["contrary", "opposite", "opposing", "opponent"], "examples": [{"es": "Al contrario de lo que pensaba, fue fácil.", "en": "Contrary to what I thought, it was easy."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "gender": null, "plural": null, "conjugations": null, "irregular": false, "register": "neutral", "reflexive": null, "ipa": "", "syllables": []}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": ["opuesto", "inverso", "diferente"], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": ["igual", "mismo"]}, "frequency": {"corpus_frequency": 23421, "band": "B1"}, "domains": ["everyday"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 1238, "word": "taxi", "display": "cab", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "A1", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Coger/tomar un taxi = to take a taxi. Parar un taxi = to hail a cab. Taxista = taxi driver. The same word in most languages. Invariable plural: los taxis.", "glosses": ["taxi", "cab"], "examples": [{"es": "Voy a pedir un taxi para llegar al aeropuerto.", "en": "I'm going to order a taxi to get to the airport."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "gender": "m", "plural": "taxis", "conjugations": null, "irregular": false, "register": "neutral", "reflexive": null, "ipa": "", "syllables": []}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": ["taxista", "coche", "uber"], "synonyms": ["cab"], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"corpus_frequency": 23114, "band": "A1"}, "domains": ["transport", "everyday"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 1239, "word": "red", "display": "network / net", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "B1", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "La red = the internet/web. Red social = social network. Red de carreteras = road network. Caer en la red = to fall into the net (literal or figurative). Short: la red (web).", "glosses": ["network", "net", "web", "internet", "grid"], "examples": [{"es": "Lo encontré buscando en la red.", "en": "I found it by searching on the web."}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "gender": "f", "plural": "redes", "conjugations": null, "irregular": false, "register": "neutral", "reflexive": null, "ipa": "", "syllables": []}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": ["internet", "conexión", "malla"], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"corpus_frequency": 23197, "band": "B1"}, "domains": ["technology", "internet", "fishing", "sport"], "register": "neutral", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
{"rank": 1240, "word": "trago", "display": "drink / sip", "pos": "noun", "difficulty": "B1", "tags": ["curated"], "notes": "Tomar un trago = to have a drink. Un trago amargo = a bitter pill (idiom). De un trago = in one gulp. Informal for any alcoholic drink in Latin America. Tragos = drinks (at a bar).", "glosses": ["drink", "sip", "gulp", "swig"], "examples": [{"es": "¿Tomamos un trago después del trabajo?", "en": "Shall we have a drink after work?"}], "linguistic": {"infinitive": null, "gender": "m", "plural": "tragos", "conjugations": null, "irregular": false, "register": "informal", "reflexive": null, "ipa": "", "syllables": []}, "relations": {"commonly_confused_with": [], "related": ["beber", "copa", "vaso", "bar"], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, "frequency": {"corpus_frequency": 22952, "band": "B1"}, "domains": ["food", "social", "everyday"], "register": "informal", "lang": "spanish", "source": "curated", "needs_review": false}
